.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt MOP 1
.Os macOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm mop
.Nd access encrypted secrets using the Mac Secure Enclave
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Cm completion
.Ar bash | zsh | fish
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
stores UTF-8 secrets in an encrypted file with a Secure Enclave key for each
approved Mac.
It requires macOS 15 or later, supported hardware, and an
interactive login session and a signed, provisioned application bundle.
Each command accessing secrets authenticates afresh
using Touch ID or the system password (Touch ID only for strict device keys).
There is no persistent unlock session.
.Pp
Secret references use
.Dl mop://vault/item/[section/]field
Components are nonempty, case-sensitive, Unicode-normalized, and
percent-encoded.
A sectionless field differs from a field in a section.
Queries and fragments are
not supported.
Logical vault names are namespaces; access permissions apply to
the entire encrypted file.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm read Ar REF Op Fl n
Print a field, appending a newline unless
.Fl n , -no-newline
is specified.
Supports the output options below.
.It Cm write Ar REF Op Fl -replace
Create one field.
Read its value through a hidden terminal prompt or UTF-8 stdin;
never supply a secret as an argument.
Stdin preserves multiline content and
trailing newlines.
The hidden prompt accepts one line up to 65,536 UTF-8 bytes.
.Fl -replace
updates an existing field and fails if it is missing.
.It Xo
.Cm list
.Op Fl -vault Ar NAME
.Op Fl -json
.Xc
List canonical references without values.
The vault filter uses a decoded,
case-sensitive name.
JSON output is an array of reference strings.
.It Cm delete Ar REF
Delete exactly the referenced field after authentication.
.It Xo
.Cm run
.Op Fl -env-file Ar FILE ...
.Op Fl -no-masking
.Fl -
.Ar COMMAND
.Op Ar ARGS ...
.Xc
Resolve environment references, then execute the supplied argument vector
without
an implicit shell.
Repeated references are fetched once.
All lookups must succeed
before execution.
The command's exit status is preserved.
.Pp
By default, separate stdout/stderr streams are filtered to replace exact,
nonempty secret values with
.Dq [concealed by mop] .
Multiline values and matches crossing buffer boundaries are supported.
Encoded
or transformed values, direct file writes, and deliberate bypasses are not
masked.
Pipes affect buffering, color, and terminal detection.
Use
.Fl -no-masking
for direct execution and full terminal/job-control behavior.
.It Cm inject Op Fl i Ar FILE
Replace
.Dq {{ mop://vault/item/[section/]field }}
placeholders.
Read stdin unless
.Fl i , -in-file
is supplied.
Supports the output options below.
All lookups complete before
output.
Substitution is literal, with no JSON, YAML, shell, or URL escaping.
.It Cm vault init Fl -recovery-file Ar FILE Op Fl -name Ar NAME Op Fl -strict-biometrics
Create an encrypted vault and a new offline recovery credential, without
overwriting existing files.
The recovery file's parent must exist.
Keep this
credential offline; it is a full alternative decryption capability.
.It Xo
.Cm vault recover
.Fl -recovery-file Ar FILE
.Op Fl -name Ar NAME
.Op Fl -strict-biometrics
.Op Fl -fingerprint Ar HASH | Fl -revision Ar HASH
.Xc
Enroll this Mac using the recovery credential and local authentication.
When
local trust is missing, supply independently verified evidence as described
under
.Cm vault trust .
.It Cm vault fingerprint
Print the vault-key fingerprint after authentication and local trust
verification.
.It Cm vault trust Fl -fingerprint Ar HASH | Fl -revision Ar HASH
Establish local trust using exactly one independently verified fingerprint or
revision hash.
Obtain the vault fingerprint from a trusted Mac, or the revision
SHA-256 from a known-good backup.
Evidence from only the suspect file is not
sufficient.
Local trust is bound to the vault path and stored outside cloud sync.
.It Cm vault conflicts
Preserve known file versions and list encrypted revision hashes.
This operation
inspects ciphertext metadata and does not authenticate or print secret values.
.It Cm vault resolve Fl -revision Ar HASH
Restore the selected revision's contents after authentication, retaining
current
device authorization and key.
Preserve known versions; never merge automatically.
Selected and current keys must satisfy local trust checks.
.It Cm device request Fl -out Ar FILE Op Fl -name Ar NAME Op Fl -strict-biometrics
Create or unlock this Mac's device key, write a new public enrollment request,
and print its fingerprint.
Compare the fingerprint through a trusted channel.
.It Cm device identity
Verify application signing and OS Keychain entitlement without authentication;
print the private Keychain access group.
.It Cm device add Fl -request Ar FILE Fl -fingerprint Ar HASH
Enroll the requested device after verifying its full fingerprint.
.It Cm device list
Print authenticated JSON containing device names and fingerprints.
.It Cm device remove Ar HASH
Revoke another device and rotate the vault key.
Old copies remain readable by
former recipients.
The current device cannot revoke itself.
Verify and pin the
new vault fingerprint on remaining Macs before reading the updated file.
.It Cm completion Ar bash | zsh | fish
Print a shell completion script to stdout.
Completes commands, flags, shell names,
and file/directory options without authentication or inspecting vault contents.
Secret references, device fingerprints, and revisions are not enumerated.
The built-in
.Fl -generate-completion-script Ar SHELL
option also generates scripts.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
Operational subcommands accept:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -vault-file Ar FILE
Select the encrypted file; overrides
.Ev MOP_VAULT_FILE .
.It Fl -state-directory Ar DIRECTORY
Select local device-key and trust storage; overrides
.Ev MOP_STATE_DIRECTORY .
Never place this directory in cloud storage.
.It Fl h , -help
Show help.
Use
.Nm help Ar command
for command-specific help.
.It Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Pp
.Cm read
and
.Cm inject
also accept:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl o , -out-file Ar FILE
Write atomically to a regular file instead of stdout.
Resolve all secrets before
creating output.
Reject symlinks and protected vault, history, key, and trust paths.
The parent directory must already exist.
.It Fl -file-mode Ar OCTAL
Output permissions, default 0600.
Accept 0000 through 0777 without special bits.
Requires
.Fl -out-file .
.It Fl f , -force
Replace an existing output file without an overwrite prompt.
Requires
.Fl -out-file .
Without this option existing destinations fail unchanged.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ev MOP_VAULT_FILE
Vault path; defaults to
.Pa ~/.mop/.mopfile .
.It Ev MOP_STATE_DIRECTORY
Local state directory; defaults to
.Pa ~/.mop .
.It Ev PATH
Executable search path used by
.Cm run .
.El
.Pp
.Cm run
reads inherited environment variables followed by each
.Fl -env-file
in order.
Later assignments win.
Dotenv accepts literal NAME=value assignments,
single/double quotes, empty values, and comments; no shell execution, export
keyword, backslash unescaping, or quoted multiline syntax.
.Pp
Only entire environment values beginning with mop:// are resolved.
.Cm run
and
.Cm inject
expand $NAME and ${NAME} once inside reference components.
Run uses the final
merged environment; inject uses the inherited environment.
Substitutions are
encoded as literal component text.
Undefined variables and malformed expressions
fail before authentication.
Use %24 for a literal dollar sign.
Other template
text, dotenv values, and fetched secrets are not expanded.
.Sh BIOMETRIC POLICY
.Fl -strict-biometrics
on vault init, vault recover, or device request creates a device key requiring
the current Touch ID enrollment, without login-password fallback.
The policy persists without repeating the flag.
Adding or removing fingerprints invalidates key access; recovery or another
enrolled device is required.
Existing non-strict keys cannot change policy in place: use a fresh state
directory, enroll the replacement, then revoke the old key.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa ~/.mop/.mopfile
Default AES-256-GCM encrypted vault.
.It Pa ~/.mop/.mopfile.history/
Preserved encrypted revisions.
Keep history with the vault when syncing.
.It Pa ~/.mop/device.json
Owner-only public device metadata and Keychain account UUID; no key blob.
The opaque enclave key is in the application-specific Data Protection Keychain.
.It Pa ~/.mop/trust/
Local vault-key trust records; never sync these with the vault.
.El
.Pp
Only vault format v3 and device metadata v2 are accepted.
Older files are unsupported; create fresh vault and state paths.
Each value has an independent key wrapped directly for each recipient.
Open/list decrypt only the index; read decrypts only the requested value.
File coordination is local, not a distributed lock. iCloud changes can
conflict;
use explicit conflict resolution.
Trust pins do not prevent all old-file replays.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "126, 127"
.It 0
Success.
.It 2
Invalid CLI, reference, dotenv, template, process, or output options.
.It 3
Authentication failed, cancelled, or unavailable.
.It 4
Secret field missing.
.It 5
Secret, enrollment, or output file already exists.
.It 6, 8
Keychain failure or missing/invalid signed application identity.
.It 7
Input/output failure or invalid UTF-8.
.It 9
Vault file missing.
.It 10
Invalid, unsupported, or unauthentic vault.
.It 11
Stale write or unresolved version conflict.
.It 12
Secure Enclave unavailable.
.It 13
Device not enrolled or initialized.
.It 14
Invalid device, fingerprint, request, or recovery credential.
.It 15
Unsafe file type, permissions, or protected output path.
.It 16
Missing or mismatched local vault-key trust.
.It 126, 127
Program cannot execute, or cannot be found.
.El
.Pp
After successful execution,
.Cm run
returns the child's exit status.
Diagnostics go to stderr without secret values.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Read a token without an appended newline:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mop read mop://personal/github/token --no-newline
.Ed
.Pp
Run GitHub CLI with an ephemeral token environment:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
GH_TOKEN=mop://personal/github/token mop run -- gh repo list
.Ed
.Pp
Generate an owner-only configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mop inject -i config.template -o config.generated --file-mode 0600
.Ed
.Pp
In Bash or zsh, pass a single-line password to sshpass on descriptor 3:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sshpass -d 3 ssh sshprofile 3< <(mop read mop://personal/sshprofile/password)
.Ed
.Pp
This avoids a long-lived password environment variable.
Process substitution is
asynchronous: SSH can start before authentication finishes, and its exit status
does not report the substitution's status.
.Pp
Generate completions without accessing secrets:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mop completion bash
mop completion zsh
mop completion fish
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bash 1 ,
.Xr fish 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr sshpass 1 ,
.Xr zsh 1
.Pp
Installation and completion setup:
.Lk https://github.com/koehn/mop#readme
.Pp
Usage examples:
.Lk https://github.com/koehn/mop/blob/main/docs/EXAMPLES.md
